 "definition": "A straight-line sequence of program instructions with one entry point and one exit and no branching in between, used in compiler analysis and optimisation.",
 "description": {
  "text": "In compiler construction, a straight-line code sequence with no branches in except at the entry and none out except at the exit. Compilers split programs into basic blocks to analyze them; they form the nodes of a control-flow graph.",
